/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  species/Dye.dat -- CASE-LOCAL: the trivalent dye anion of Bowen &
  Mohammad's CA30 experiments (W.R. Bowen, A.W. Mohammad, "Diafiltration
  by nanofiltration: prediction and optimization", AIChE J. 44 (1998)
  1799), as Geraldes & Alves (J. Membr. Sci. 321 (2008) 172-182, their
  section 4.1) carry it into NanoFiltran: charge -3, Stokes radius
  0.63 nm, D 0.36e-9 m2/s -- the DYE3- row of the ion database NanoFiltran
  ships (bin/curate/nanofiltran/shipped/IONS.XLS), which cites Bowen &
  Mohammad.  The paper does not name the dye; neither does this record.

  ONLY what the pore model reads: a charge, a Stokes radius, a free-
  solution diffusivity.  No thermochemistry, no molar mass: nothing here
  prices an energy or converts a mass, and a number nobody stated is not
  written in.  Its radius equals the CA30 pore radius (0.63 nm), so
  lambda = 1: the dye does not enter the pore (the DSPM-DE law's steric
  partition at lambda >= 1, as NanoFiltran's) and is rejected completely;
  it matters through the film and the electroneutrality it imposes there.
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType modelSpecies;
schemaVersion 1;

name    Dye;
formula     "Dye-3";
charge  -3;

transport
{
radius { value 6.30e-10; unit m;}
D0     { value 3.60e-10; unit m2/s;}
}
